# Emitted by tsc, which writes exactly these bytes. With core.autocrlf=true a
# checkout would rewrite their line endings, so the compiler output would
# never match what git expects and these files would stand as modified after
# every build, with an empty diff. Left alone in both directions, the round
# trip is exact - which is what the build stamp needs to mean anything.
WWCP_WebAPI/HTTPRoot/defaults/defaults.js      -text
WWCP_WebAPI/HTTPRoot/defaults/defaults.js.map  -text
